      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel hopeless when the crushing weight of genetics and family history seems to make resistance feel pointless. However, the concept of acceptance often means accepting the biology to recognize that healing is still possible, rather than accepting doom. Choosing to rest and focus on self-preservation is different from stopping the fight entirely, and your family's history is powerful but not a destiny written in stone.",
